; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Pythagoras Tree
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     recursion, squares, Pythagoras, FILLED, tree
; SUMMARY:  Builds a tree out of squares, with two smaller squares on top of every square.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   On top of a square sits a right angled triangle, and on its two
;   short sides sit two smaller squares. By Pythagoras, their areas
;   add up to the area of the big one. Repeat on every square and a
;   tree appears, brown at the trunk and green at the leaves.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change :lean near the bottom to make a lopsided tree.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * the Pythagorean theorem in a picture
;   * SIN and COS to size the two children for any angle
;   * FILLED squares that the turtle walks around
;   * blending two colors by the depth of the recursion
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Set :lean to 30 or 60 for a tree blowing in the wind.
;   * Raise the depth to 12. How many squares is that?
;   * Put the pen down (and leave out FILLED) to see only outlines.
; ============================================================

; BLEND gives a color between brown (depth = max) and leaf green
; (depth = 1). :t goes from 0 to 1 as the squares get smaller.
to blend :depth
  localmake "t 1 - :depth / :maxdepth
  output (list 110 - 60 * :t 70 + 150 * :t 40 + 20 * :t)
end

; BOX paints one square to the right of the turtle and comes back.
to box :size :depth
  filled blend :depth [repeat 4 [forward :size right 90]]
end

; PTREE starts at the bottom left corner of a square, facing up the
; left edge, and finishes in the same place.
to ptree :size :depth
  if :depth = 0 [stop]
  box :size :depth
  ; Climb to the top left corner and lean left for the first child.
  forward :size
  left :lean
  ptree :size * cos :lean :depth - 1
  ; Walk across the first child's base to the tip of the triangle,
  ; then face along the base of the second child.
  right 90
  forward :size * cos :lean
  ptree :size * sin :lean :depth - 1
  ; Retrace the steps exactly, in reverse.
  back :size * cos :lean
  left 90
  right :lean
  back :size
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [230 240 250]
make "lean 45
make "maxdepth 11
; The pen stays up: FILLED still paints each square, and without
; outlines the leaves blend into soft clumps of green.
penup setxy -45 -270 setheading 0
ptree 90 :maxdepth
